1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:03,210
What's this for?

2
00:00:03,210 --> 00:00:06,200
Just because. How's the baby?

3
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:07,270
Fast asleep.

4
00:00:07,270 --> 00:00:11,300
I'm sorry I missed him. I had to work late.

5
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:13,730
What are the flowers for, Richard?

6
00:00:13,730 --> 00:00:18,060
Five years of happiness. Happy anniversary.

7
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:20,300
But our anniversary isn't until Saturday.

8
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:21,400
I couldn't wait.

9
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:25,300
Besides, we are not going to be here Saturday.

10
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:26,800
We're not?

11
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:27,850
Uh-uh.

12
00:00:27,850 --> 00:00:31,700
Where are we going to be?

13
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:35,300
If you had your choice of all the places in the world.

14
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:39,740
where would you choose to spend our anniversary?

15
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:41,900
The Watermill Inn.

16
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:44,180
I loved that place when we went on our honeymoon.

17
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:47,900
Perfect! You picked the right place.

18
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:49,800
I don't understand.

19
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:51,500
You and I, Mrs. Stewart,

20
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:55,300
are going to spend a second honeymoon at the Watermill Inn.

21
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:59,300
Oh, Richard! That's wonderful, but--

22
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:00,400
No buts.

23
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:01,200
What about the baby?

24
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:02,720
Aren't we taking the baby on our honeymoon?

25
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:04,100
Absolutely not.

26
00:01:04,100 --> 00:01:06,300
The world's greatest grandmother, Mrs. Ellen Stewart,

27
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:09,610
has agreed to take care of him for the weekend.

28
00:01:09,610 --> 00:01:12,500
Richard, isn't that too much to ask of your mother?

29
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:16,890
Too much? She loves taking care of Max.

30
00:01:16,890 --> 00:01:21,300
But ... I'll miss him.

31
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:23,380
Well, we'll phone every hour,

32
00:01:23,380 --> 00:01:25,800
and you can listen to him over the phone.

33
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:27,670
Come on, Mar.

34
00:01:27,670 --> 00:01:30,300
It's time you and I had a romantic weekend alone together.

35
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:37,800
We've earned it. What do you say?

36
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:40,300
It does sound tempting.

37
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:43,000
You're right. We've earned it.

38
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:48,600
Great! I'll make a reservation right now.

39
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:49,400
Remember that wonderful little balcony

40
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:51,400
where we had our meals ...

41
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:54,200
with a view of the Hudson River?

42
00:01:54,200 --> 00:02:05,600
How could I forget?

43
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:08,800
Hello. Is Mrs. Montefiore there?

44
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:11,400
Ah. She's out.

45
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:13,100
Yes. This is Richard Stewart.

46
00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:17,000
My wife and I spent our honeymoon at the inn.

47
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:18,800
No, we didn't leave anything in the room.

48
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:20,100
It's five years ago.

49
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:23,000
We'd like to make a reservation for this weekend.

50
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:29,400
Yes, a double room, please. What?

51
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:36,800
Are you sure? But ... OK.

52
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:38,400
Nothing available.

53
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:40,500
Wait! Don't hang up!

54
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:44,800
Can you recommend someplace nice--someplace nearby?

55
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:55,000
Uh--hold it. Old Country Inn?

56
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:01,030
Right. And the phone number?

57
00:03:01,030 --> 00:03:06,800
555-2420. Thank you. 555-2420

58
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:08,500
He says there's another inn

59
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:11,900
just half a mile down the road from the Watermill.

60
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:15,600
It won't be the same, but what do you say?

61
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:15,800
Well ...

62
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:18,500
My mom is available to baby-sit this weekend.

63
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:21,600
Well, OK. See if they have a room.

64
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:30,700
Right!

65
00:03:30,700 --> 00:03:33,600
Hello. Is this the Old Country Inn?

66
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:35,200
Yes. This is Richard Stewart.

67
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:38,100
The desk clerk at the Watemill suggested your inn.

68
00:03:38,100 --> 00:03:40,300
Would you happen to have a room for two availbale

69
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:42,200
this weekend?

70
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:43,500
Something really nice.

71
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:47,700
My wife and I are celebrating our fifth anniversary.

72
00:03:47,700 --> 00:03:52,710
Yes. I'll hold. He's checking. You do?

73
00:03:52,710 --> 00:03:56,800
Great! What is the daily rate?

74
00:03:56,800 --> 00:03:59,000
That's fine. Thank you.

75
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:03,460
Yes, we'll be arriving by car about ten o'clock Friday night.

76
00:04:03,460 --> 00:04:11,900
Stewart. S-t-e-w-a-r-t. Thank you.

77
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:16,400
Done! You and I, Mrs. Stewart.

78
00:04:16,400 --> 00:04:21,600
are going to have a wonderful, romantic weekend!

79
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:24,600
Richard, that's the baby. Richard
